  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;Certificate of Lawfulness for a proposed\r\ndevelopment is refused under Article 3(5) of the General Permitted Development Order\r\n(GPDO) is based on the principle that GPDO rights cannot be applied to land or\r\nbuildings where there are existing breaches of planning control. Article 3(5)\r\nof the GPDO specifies that permitted development rights are not available for\r\nland that is in an &lt;i&gt;unlawful&lt;/i&gt; condition due to unauthorised structures or\r\nuses.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;The proposed height of the outbuilding is higher than 2.5m and the outbuilding would not be set in by 2m from the side boundaries. As such,&amp;nbsp; the proposal is not within the tolerances of Schedule 2, Part 1 Class E of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
